Subject: [PATCH 027/260] [ae-patch] Reject navigation.openExternal with
 PopupBlocked when the browser blocks the new tab

Review of https://github.com/analyticendeavors/omnigent-ae/pull/58
(Claude and Codex, 2026-09-27): the handler opened with
window.open(url, "_blank", "noopener,noreferrer") and ignored the result.
With noopener, window.open returns null even on success, and the open runs
one MessagePort hop after the tap, where iOS Safari may block it, so a
blocked tab looked like success and the extension never offered a fallback.

aeOpenExternalWindow (web/src/lib/aeExternalUrls.ts) now opens without
noopener, clears the new window's opener at once (the protection noopener
gave), and throws ExtensionHostServiceError("PopupBlocked") when
window.open returns null. Native shells keep upstream's noopener call:
their window-open policy routes the link to the system browser and reports
null regardless (as followLinkWithPopupFallback in ChatMarkdown.tsx notes).
The handler's edit is the import and one line; the URL allowlist and the
GitHub matcher are unchanged.

Tests: the GitHub cases now get a window back and check its opener is
cleared; a null return rejects with PopupBlocked; an Electron shell keeps
the noopener call. Upstream's handed-out case mocks a returned window and
expects the two-argument open.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
